From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 112/112] PC5: the hardware cursor follows the pointer between
 presents (Wine patch 0980)

A game that draws only when something changes (Age of Empires II HD's menus)
lost its pointer: VideoOut's hardware cursor followed it only at a present,
and was hidden once a desktop frame had shown, while the desktop's frames with
the cursor drawn in are left out as empty. win32u now hands each move, new
image or hiding to libvulkan.prx's pw_videoout_cursor_follow, which shows it
unless a desktop frame is what shows. Wine patch 0999 is the same on top of
it, and hides the followed cursor when unused too.
