 console's pointer fades, both where it draws the cursor over the screen
 itself and where Vulkan frames get it from VideoOut's hardware cursor
-(patch 0740). The next move (the mouse,
+(patch 0740, and between presents patch 0980). The next move (the mouse,
 the touchpad or a stick working as a mouse, even against an edge) or
 click shows it again at once, and so does the game moving it to another
 place itself (SetCursorPos): Grim Dawn moves its pointer by the
@@ -24,9 +24,9 @@ GetCursorInfo and everything else still see it as shown.
 
 WINE_PS5_CURSOR_IDLE_MS sets the time in milliseconds. Unset or 0 never
 hides it: only a game that asks for it changes.
